<item><title>Eswatini Cabinet backs judicial inquiry into corruption</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/eswatini-cabinet-backs-judicial-inquiry-into-corruption-a1ed8a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/eswatini-cabinet-backs-judicial-inquiry-into-corruption-a1ed8a/</guid><category>Eswatini</category><description>Finance minister Neal Rijkenberg said estimated monthly losses to corruption have risen from E80 million to E90 million.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:49:03 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/eswatini-cabinet-backs-judicial-inquiry-into-corruption-a1ed8a/share.jpg" length="41525" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/eswatini-cabinet-backs-judicial-inquiry-into-corruption-a1ed8a/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Eswatini soldiers walk in support of national HIV response</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/eswatini-soldiers-walk-in-support-of-national-hiv-response-e9c743/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/eswatini-soldiers-walk-in-support-of-national-hiv-response-e9c743/</guid><category>Eswatini</category><description>The defence force held the solidarity walk from Matsapha to Nokwane Headquarters on 26 November, urging testing and continued treatment.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:47:16 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sz.jpg" length="32835" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sz.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Eswatini secures air cargo licence as security compliance reaches 85%</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/eswatini-secures-air-cargo-licence-as-security-compliance-72d7b3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sz/eswatini-secures-air-cargo-licence-as-security-compliance-72d7b3/</guid><category>Eswatini</category><description>Principal Secretary Thulani Mkhaliphi said the licence was obtained in the week before he spoke, after the country raised aviation security compliance from about 35%.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:32:44 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sz.jpg" length="32835" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sz.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
